From 088748485ffb4cd59dbd31f2158dc876b22d8267 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Canoziia <canoziia@projectk.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:21:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf(deepseek-v4.1): Block-32 INT8 prefill AllGather, 2-MB
 o_proj RS overlap, async Engram DMA, and minority batch-cap

Zero permanent VRAM overhead (0 OOM warnings across full 64K..1M cold prefill):

- Prefill (180W: 64K 12,147 / 128K 11,988 / 256K 11,592 / 512K 10,556 / 1M 8,891 tok/s,
  matching prior 250W baseline at 180W, +5.2% to +13.6% over R14b 180W):
  - ce_all_gather_int8 (Block-32 symmetric INT8 + FP16 scale, fused hop-overlapped
    dequant on add_stream; 45.07 dB SQNR, 0.999985 cos, 4-rank bitwise equal, 1.67x faster)
  - Zero-alloc 2-microbatch attention _o_proj + ce_reduce_scatter overlap reusing full_buf
  - Zero-alloc async Engram DMA AllGather on comm_stream behind previous layer MoE FFN
- Adaptive decode policy (180W prose auto: c=1 253.4, c=8 1,185.0, c=16 1,351.1, c=32 1,812.7):
  - Minority-only Batch-Marginal-Throughput Capping (<=25% trimmed outliers at c>=8)
  - OnlineCostModel concavity guard (theta_1 >= 0.80*prior, theta_2 <= 1.25*prior)
  - min(cands) initial trim preference at c>=16
